      "type": "about",
      "tabLabel": "About",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Ace-To-Six Lowball",
          "subtitle": "London 6-4 Low",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Ace-To-Six Lowball is a lowball variant in which aces are low, but straights and flushes count against the hand."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Ace-to-six lowball developed in home games on the eastern United States and in London and European poker circles as a stricter lowball form."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Two to eight players. As in other five-card draw lowball games; deal and betting follow the same structure as California lowball. With more than six players the deck can run short on the draw and house rules may allow shuffling the muck for replacement cards."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Standard 52-card deck; optional joker bug in some house rules."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deck, chips, dealer button, and blind markers if blind structure is used."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal 5 cards face-down to each player."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Variations",
          "subtitle": "Known ways this game changes",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "style": "unordered",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Single Draw: One draw round and two main betting rounds."
                },
                {
                  "text": "Triple Draw: Three draw rounds with additional betting rounds."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
